      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Need for non-cardiac surgery is a common event during the follow-up of patients treated drug-eluting stenting. The eventual associated risks of complications (bleeding and stent thrombosis) are relatively low. Larger clinical studies are needed to better delineate the optimal management of this population."
